e retailer in the United States, the United Kingdom, and Canada. The company operates in two segments, Vehicle Operations and Financing Operations. It offers a range of products and services fulfilling the entire vehicle ownership lifecycle, including new and used vehicles, financing and insurance products, and aftersales automotive repair and maintenance services. The company provides its products and services through a network of physical locations, e-commerce platforms, captive finance solutions, fleet management offerings, and other synergistic adjacencies. Lithia Motors, Inc. was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Medford, Oregon.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Bryan B. DeBoer | Chairman & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2015)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 30K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $193 of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Lithia Motors, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $6.4B market cap on $37.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 7% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 15% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $6M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.44\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 15.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Cyclical peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 47% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Lithia Motors (NYSE:LAD) and Five Below (NASDAQ:FIVE)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/contrasting-lithia-motors-nyselad-and-five-below-nasdaqfive.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490183.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (LAD)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/16/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_LAD_111226073802_1794487082.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794487082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Precision Trading with Lithia Motors Inc. (LAD) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Precision_Trading_with_Lithia_Motors_Inc._LAD_Risk_Zones_110226074402_1793623442.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793623442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Lithia Motors (NYSE:LAD) Gaining Pace After Raising Its Dividend?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/is-lithia-motors-nyselad-gaining-pace-after-raising-its-dividend","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793615100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Zacks Research Reduces Earnings Estimates for Lithia Motors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/za