apex roughly matches depreciation (1.1x, 0.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 23, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.2%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $396K sold).","It returns 15.4% a year to shareholders (14.6% in buybacks and 1.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 6.0% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 16 consecutive years, raising it 13.7% a year over the last five.","Short interest is elevated at 12.9% of the float, 4.3 days to cover."],"people":["With about 30,000 employees, each generates about $1.3M of revenue, 3.3x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 20.7% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $5.2M (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":66,"head":"Invest: trades 47% below fair value of $562; revenue grew 23.5%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Composite 46, above the 39 line (gates 12/26)","Trades 47% below fair value of $562","Revenue grew 23.5%/yr over 5y","P/E 8.6x vs sector 18.8x","15 analysts' mean target $391 (+32%)"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 5.0x","Piotroski F-score 3/9","P/FCF 1105.3x vs sector 16.7x"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":478.03,"vc":{"base":562.39,"base_src":"dcf","bear":281.25,"bull":705.29,"alt_median":372.77,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.2152,"dispersion":0.4457,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (45% dispersion)","DCF is 122% above the other models' median ($373)"]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[147.93,235.55,281.25,313.18,339.37,358.68,378.43,393.27,414.49,437.01,464.08,482.63,505.04,528.89,559.58,585.42,620.11,662